      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n\n## Column Mapping\n- department: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- department name: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- Mathematics (Course 18): SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- subject grade type: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.GRADE_TYPE\n- grade type: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.GRADE_TYPE\n- letter graded: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.GRADE_TYPE\n- subject is offered in the current academic year: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR\n- number of such subjects: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n- minimum total units: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\n- top 10 departments by number of subjects offered in the 2022 academic year: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.ACADEMIC_YEAR, SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n- excluding Political Science: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- degree-granting departments: SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n- number of subjects offered by that department in 2022: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.ACADEMIC_YEAR, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n\n## Join Keys\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n\n## Domain Knowledge\n- \"math\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\"\n- \"degree-granting\" is predicated by \"TABLE.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y'\"\n- \"Course 18\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_CODE = '18'\"\n- \"Political Science\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_CODE = '17'\"\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For each department and subject grade type where the subject is offered in the current academic year, is letter graded, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the number of subjects and the minimum total units.\n```sql\nSELECT d.DEPARTMENT_NAME, c.GRADE_TYPE, COUNT(c.SUBJECT_ID) AS subject_count, MIN(c.TOTAL_UNITS) AS min_total_units FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT d JOIN COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED c ON d.DEPARTMENT_CODE = c.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE c.IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR = 'Y' AND c.GRADE_TYPE = 'L' AND d.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' AND d.DEPARTMENT_CODE = '18' GROUP BY d.DEPARTMENT_NAME, c.GRADE_TYPE;\n```\n2. List the top 10 departments by the number of subjects offered in the 2022 academic year, showing each department's name and the count of subjects, but exclude the Political Science department (Course 17) from the results and only include departments that grant degrees.\n```sql\nSELECT SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME, COUNT(COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID) AS subject_count FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT JOIN COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ON SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE = COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2022 AND SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE <> '17' GROUP BY SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY subject_count DESC LIMIT 10;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor each department and subject grade type where the subject is offered in the current academic year, is letter graded, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the department name, grade type, the number of such subjects, the minimum total units, and, if the department is among the top 10 departments by number of subjects offered in the 2022 academic year (excluding Political Science and only including degree-granting departments), also provide the number of subjects offered by that department in 2022. Do not return any rounded answers."
